318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (        he Tech-O-Nicks recently hosted a successful six-day online workshop on python from 22nd to 27th July, designed to equip students with a solid foundation in Python programming. Presented by the student instructors Parthiv Bania, Rishav Prasad, Anirudha Ghosh, Rajat Mandal and Utsav Pal, the event drew a huge number of eager participants, from complete beginners to those looking to refine their existing skills.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The workshop kicked off by focusing on the fundamentals, ensuring a solid base for all participants. The initial sessions were dedicated to understanding Python's syntax, its various data types, and the essential control structures that form the backbone of any program. Participants learned to write simple yet effective code, mastering if-else statements, for loops, and while loops. The interactive nature of the online sessions, which included live coding demos and immediate Q&A, made it easy for students to grasp these core principles and apply them in real-time. This foundational stage was crucial, as it set the stage for the more complex topics to come.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This session was particularly transformative, as it moved the students from writing simple scripts to thinking in terms of building organized, scalable applications. The final two days were the highlight of the workshop, dedicated to putting theory into practice. The sessions moved beyond the basics to introduce participants to popular Python libraries used in data analysis and web development. Students got hands-on experience with tasks like file handling, data parsing, and building simple web applications. This practical component was a game-changer, as it showed students the immense power and versatility of Python in real-world scenarios. Feedback from attendees was overwhelmingly positive. Many appreciated the interactive format, noting that the balance between theory and practice helped build both understanding and confidence. The enthusiasm and creativity displayed were a clear reflection of how deeply the students had benefitted from the experience. The Code-A-Thon competition towards the end of the workshop gave students a platform to apply their skills to practical challenges, making the learning experience both rewarding and memorable. It took place on the final day, on 27th July. This finale was not just a celebration of their new skills but also a glimpse into the endless possibilities that Python offers, from data science to web development. In recognition of every learner's effort, Tech-O-Nicks will also present certificates of participation.The Python Mastery Workshop was not just about learning a programming language; it was about promoting a culture of coding curiosity and problem-solving. The online format ensured that students could participate from anywhere, making the workshop accessible to a broader audience. The success of this event reinforces Tech-O-Nicks' commitment to empowering students with valuable skills for their academic and professional careers. The club is already looking forward to hosting more such workshops in the future, aiming to cover other cutting-edge technologies and continue supporting the growth of our student community.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
